# Dataset License and Attribution

## 1. Primary Dataset

**Dataset:** RGB — Retrieval-Augmented Generation Benchmark

**Official Repository:** https://github.com/chen700564/RGB

**Research Paper:** [Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation](https://doi.org/10.1609/AAAI.V38I16.29728)

**Authors:** Jiawei Chen, Hongyu Lin, Xianpei Han, and Le Sun.

**Publication:** AAAI 2024.

## 2. Dataset License

The RGB repository specifies the following license:

**Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).**

Official license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

This license generally requires:

- **Attribution:** Credit the original authors and provide the source.
- **NonCommercial:** Do not use the licensed material for commercial purposes.
- **ShareAlike:** Distribute adaptations under the same or a compatible license as required by the license terms.

Users must review the original repository and license before downloading, modifying, or redistributing the dataset.

## 3. Dataset Usage in This Research

The RGB benchmark will be used as the primary evaluation source for this research project.

Planned usage:

1. Inspect the original English benchmark structure.
2. Select a documented evaluation subset.
3. Preserve original question IDs and reference answers.
4. Generate controlled irrelevant and contradictory context variants.
5. Evaluate BM25, dense, and hybrid retrieval configurations.
6. Report experimental results with appropriate attribution.

Original benchmark data and project-generated experimental data will be maintained separately.

## 4. Dataset Redistribution Policy

This repository will not redistribute the original RGB dataset files.

Users should obtain the dataset directly from the official repository and comply with its license.

The repository may contain:

- Dataset download instructions.
- Original benchmark attribution.
- Dataset IDs and references.
- Original experimental configurations.
- Original code for dataset processing.
- Project-generated metadata and evaluation results, subject to applicable third-party rights.

Derived dataset materials will not be published automatically. Their redistribution will be reviewed against the upstream license.

## 5. Synthetic Data and Noise Injection

This research introduces controlled context corruption.

Two noise categories will be evaluated:

### Irrelevant Passages

Passages that do not provide useful evidence for answering the corresponding question.

### Contradictory Passages

Synthetic passages containing claims that conflict with identifiable original evidence.

Each generated passage should maintain:

- Original question ID.
- Source passage ID.
- Noise category.
- Noise severity.
- Original factual claim, where applicable.
- Generated passage.
- Verification status.

Synthetic passages must be clearly identified as generated research artifacts and must not be presented as authentic RGB benchmark documents.

## 6. Attribution

When referencing the RGB benchmark, use the following citation:

Chen, J., Lin, H., Han, X., & Sun, L. (2024). *Benchmarking Large Language Models in Retrieval-Augmented Generation*. Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence.

https://doi.org/10.1609/AAAI.V38I16.29728

Official repository:

https://github.com/chen700564/RGB

## 7. Separation of Project and Dataset Licenses

This project distinguishes between two types of intellectual property:

| Component | Applicable license |
|---|---|
| Original project implementation | MIT License |
| RGB benchmark | CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 |
| Third-party papers | Their respective copyright and usage terms |
| Third-party datasets | Their respective licenses |
| Project-generated experimental outputs | Subject to applicable source-data rights and third-party terms |

The MIT License applies only to original implementation code created for this project.

It does not replace, override, or grant additional permissions for the RGB benchmark or other third-party materials.

## 8. Research Integrity

- Original benchmark labels will not be silently modified.
- All dataset transformations will be documented.
- Generated noise will be distinguishable from original benchmark content.
- Dataset sources and versions will be recorded.
- Experimental results will be reported honestly.
- No dataset licensing permission will be assumed beyond the published terms.

